Examine the polynomial curve shown below.
Which description correctly identifies its degree parity and the sign of its leading coefficient?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.5) -- (0,1.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.1:2.1,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{-0.3*(\x*\x-2)*(\x*\x-2)+1.2});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For the polynomial function sketched below, which description correctly identifies its degree parity and the sign of its leading coefficient?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.2:2.2,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.4*(\x+1.5)*\x*(\x-1.5)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
